Text: "Formulation is the mathematical language embedded in structural sections.
This section covers lexical forms, declarations and type statements, operators,
precedence, expressions, aliases, and labels. Different structural positions
select different formulation parsers, so each page identifies where its syntax
is valid rather than implying that every phrase is a general expression."
Id: "d1992ffa-56e1-4962-9300-f8147a49e2f6"
